# Docking Report — Trametes versicolor (Control)

## Project Halo | Phase 4

## Setup
- Structure: ESMFold prediction, Trametes versicolor laccase (519 aa)
- Ligand: C.I. Reactive Black 5 (PubChem CID 135442967), target azo dye
- Tool: CB-Dock2, Auto Blind Docking
- Copper-binding loop region of interest: SER 82 - GLN 104

## Top Pockets

| Pocket | Score (kcal/mol) | Overlap with loop (82-104)? |
|---|---|---|
| C1 | -8.3 | None |
| C2 | -8.0 | None |

Full cavity scan (21 pockets total, see raw CB-Dock2 output): no pocket showed direct residue overlap with the 82-104 loop range. Closest pockets sit outside this range on both sides.

## Interpretation

No meaningful overlap found between the top-ranked or lower-ranked docking pockets and the defined copper-binding loop region. Top scores were closely clustered (0.3 kcal/mol apart), a pattern previously identified during tool testing as a sign of low confidence in any single pocket assignment, rather than a clear, dominant binding site.

An attempt to cross-reference these results against the literature-defined T1 catalytic site (approximately His394/395, His457/458, Cys452/453 in prior crystallographic studies) surfaced a residue-numbering discrepancy between this structure and the published reference data, likely due to signal peptide inclusion differences. This was not resolved within the scope of this analysis. See [t1-site-numbering-limitation.md](../notes/t1-site-numbering-limitation.md).

## Verdict

**Inconclusive.** Docking alone does not provide clear evidence either supporting or contradicting the project hypothesis for the control enzyme. Reported as an honest limitation rather than a confirmed negative result.
